{"availability":"available","full":"ODINN-SciML/ODINN.jl","name":"ODINN.jl","description":"SciML glacier model","category":"Education","language":"Julia","stars":93,"forks":16,"created":"2021-03-17T16:12:29Z","updated":"2026-10-08T20:41:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://odinn-sciml.github.io/ODINN.jl/","topics":["climate","cryosphere","differential-equations","glaciers","julia","scientific-machine-learning","sciml"],"demo":"https://odinn-sciml.github.io/ODINN.jl/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T01:06:37.257Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T01:06:37.257Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T01:06:37.257Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T21:24:58.162Z","stars":93,"forks":16},{"at":"2026-10-10T01:06:37.257Z","stars":93,"forks":16}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["For a detailed description of the model and the application of Universal Differential Equations to glacier ice flow modelling, take a look at our recent publication at Geoscientific Model Development.","Global glacier evolution model using Universal Differential Equations to model and discover processes of climate-glacier interactions.","ODINN.jl uses neural networks and differential equations in order to combine mechanistic models describing glacier physical processes (e.g. ice creep, basal sliding, surface mass balance) with machine learning. Neural networks are used to learn parts of the equations. ODINN uses the Open Global Glacier Model (OGGM, Maussion et al., 2019) through Gungnir as a basic framework to retrieve all the topographical and climate data for the initial state of the simulations. Then, all the simulations and processing are performed in Julia, benefitting from its high performance and the SciML ecosystem."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ODINN-SciML/ODINN.jl/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"564faa530ee24b2a2a0fe8d518e353fcae4874b6f21c400620d70f6f4d127dfa","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T21:24:58.29